<title>TURKEY: Turk grain board not in Saudi barley tender.</title>
<headline>Turk grain board not in Saudi barley tender.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's state grain board (TMO) said on Wednesday it did not participate in a Saudi Arabian tender under which the Arab nation will buy 500,000 tonnes of feed barley.  </p>
<p>&quot;We didn't make any bids for the Saudi tender,&quot; said an official from the TMO.</p>
<p>Grain traders confirmed on Wednesday Saudi Arabia's purchase of 500,000 tonnes of barley through the tender. Details were still awaited.</p>
<p>They said other potential suppliers included the European Union and Canada.</p>
<p>--Ercan Ersoy, Ankara newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
